// == TRACK 4 - LAYER 0 - FOUNDATION ==========================================
// "LIGHTCYCLE". The neo-racing track: Tron, a grid at speed, something chasing.
//
// The other three tracks are songs. This one is an ENGINE. Every decision below
// trades harmonic interest for forward motion, because the feeling being chased
// is velocity, and velocity comes from repetition plus a pulse that never lets
// go — not from a chord progression doing something clever.
//
// MODE: A PHRYGIAN (A Bb C D E F G). The flat 2nd is the whole identity. Track 1
// is A Aeolian and track 3 is A Dorian, so the tonic is shared and the tracks
// stay interchangeable, but Bb against A is a semitone the other two cannot
// make. It reads as menace at speed rather than sadness.
//
// A Phrygian is the F-major collection, which puts this track ONE accidental
// from Neon (C) and one from Darksynth (Bb) on the circle of fifths. `music.gd`
// rotates along that circle, so this stem's key is load-bearing for how the
// track changes sound, not just for how it sounds alone.
//
// FORM (8 cycles = 16s @ cps 0.5). Only THREE chord changes in sixteen seconds,
// where track 3 has eight. That is deliberate: a racing track that keeps
// modulating feels like it is braking.
//   A  Am  Am  Bb  Bb     i - i - bII - bII    the Phrygian lean, held
//   B  Am  Am  G   F      i - i - bVII - bVI   a descent that falls back to A
setcps(0.5)
stack(
  // THE ENGINE. True 16ths with a HOLE on the downbeat sixteenth of every beat.
  //
  // The previous version claimed "straight 16ths, an octave stab on every 4th"
  // and did not do that. `[a1*12 a2*4]` is a bracket of TWO elements, so each
  // took HALF THE BAR: twelve a1 across beats 1-2 (0.0833s apart — sextuplets)
  // and four a2 across beats 3-4 (eighths). Against straight 16th hats that is
  // 3-against-2 for half of every bar, and the pulse rate changing at the
  // halfway point is why the engine lurched instead of pulling. Caught by
  // reading the events sidecar, not the code — same discipline that caught the
  // slowcat bug in gotcha 3, one level of nesting further down.
  //
  // The rest on each downbeat does two jobs. It is the only rhythmic identity
  // this layer has that the 16th hats do not already own — everything else in
  // the track is a full grid, so the holes are the shape. And it IS the
  // sidechain: superdough has no compressor, but a bass that is simply absent
  // where the kick lands pumps for free. That is how the machines this genre
  // was built on did it, years before sidechaining was a technique.
  //
  // The octave lift moves to beats 3 and 4 only, so the bar has a front half
  // and a back half without changing pulse rate to say so.
  //
  // Resonant low-pass rather than a static one: the sweep is slow enough
  // (one pass per 8-bar loop) that it reads as ACCELERATION rather than as a
  // filter effect, which is the oldest trick in the genre and still the best.
  note(`<[[~ a1 a1 a1]  [~ a1 a1 a1]  [~ a1 a1 a2]  [~ a1 a1 a2]]
         [[~ a1 a1 a1]  [~ a1 a1 a1]  [~ a1 a1 a2]  [~ a1 a1 a2]]
         [[~ bb1 bb1 bb1] [~ bb1 bb1 bb1] [~ bb1 bb1 bb2] [~ bb1 bb1 bb2]]
         [[~ bb1 bb1 bb1] [~ bb1 bb1 bb1] [~ bb1 bb1 bb2] [~ bb1 bb1 bb2]]
         [[~ a1 a1 a1]  [~ a1 a1 a1]  [~ a1 a1 a2]  [~ a1 a1 a2]]
         [[~ a1 a1 a1]  [~ a1 a1 a1]  [~ a1 a1 a2]  [~ a1 a1 a2]]
         [[~ g1 g1 g1]  [~ g1 g1 g1]  [~ g1 g1 g2]  [~ g1 g1 g2]]
         [[~ f1 f1 f1]  [~ f1 f1 f1]  [~ f1 f1 f2]  [~ f1 f1 f2]]>`)
    .s("sawtooth")
    .lpf(sine.range(380, 1250).slow(8)).lpq(9)
    .distort("1.18:.5")
    // 0.30, not the 0.42 this used before the waveshaper went on. distort()
    // multiplies BEFORE its post-gain divides, and measured 1.39x net here —
    // at 0.72 the render clipped flat at 1.00 and the build normalised it down,
    // which loses the transient rather than the level.
    // Set by meter against the siblings' bass stems (-20.5 to -23.3 dBFS RMS),
    // not by ear: the waveshaper compresses, so written gain and rendered level
    // stopped tracking each other the moment distort() went on.
    .gain(0.19).release(0.035),

  // A single sustained fifth underneath, no third. Power-chord voicing, because
  // a triad here would state the mode and the point of Phrygian at speed is
  // that you feel the Bb arrive without being told what it is. Very quiet: it
  // is glue, not a pad.
  note("<[a2,e3] [a2,e3] [bb2,f3] [bb2,f3] [a2,e3] [a2,e3] [g2,d3] [f2,c3]>")
    .s("sawtooth").lpf(700).lpq(2)
    .gain(0.085).attack(0.3).release(1.2).room(0.4).size(0.8)
)
